sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/active-inference-morphogenesis-falsifiable--claude-opus-5-5--3> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Craniofacial remodelling: error-proportional correction vs hardwired movement" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/active-inference-morphogenesis-falsifiable> ;
    dct:description "Xenopus 'Picasso' tadpoles, with organs experimentally displaced, remodel toward normal craniofacial geometry (Vandenberg et al. 2012; Pinet et al. 2019). A fixed-target active-inference model with Gaussian precision predicts that each organ's correction velocity is proportional to its displacement from the target, giving exponential relaxation and a rate independent of the direction of displacement. A hardwired-movement alternative (organs migrate a fixed program regardless of start) predicts velocity independent of displacement. Using organ positions reported or measurable in these papers' figures at multiple stages, estimate for each organ the regression of displacement change on initial displacement. Pre-registered: the active-inference model is supported if the slope is negative with exponential-fit R² ≥ 0.6, and refuted if velocity is independent of displacement (slope CI including 0) or if organs overshoot the target systematically, which a fixed-precision gradient flow cannot produce." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "Whether correction velocity scales with displacement (supporting fixed-target error correction) or not (supporting hardwired programs), per organ, with model-comparison weights. This is a risky prediction the fixed model can fail." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: Published figures give too few time points or individuals per stage (fewer than 3 stages or 10 tadpoles), making slopes unidentifiable; or any proportional-correction result is shared by non-inferential gradient models, so it supports a class of models rather than active inference specifically (this must be stated in the interpretation)." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/data-test" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Pre-register both models' predictions and the statistics. 2. Extract organ positions over developmental stages from the published figures and supplementary data, with landmark definitions. 3. Fit the displacement-dependent and displacement-independent models; compare by AICc. 4. Check for overshoot; report verdicts per organ." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): hard" ;
    skos:note "Missing: Individual-level trajectory data are not published as tables; figure extraction is limited and new time-lapse imaging would be decisive." ;
    skos:note "Tool: morphometrics" ;
    skos:note "Tool: image-analysis" ;
    skos:note "Tool: data-test" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-place-03> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-place-04> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2019-boundary-15> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-girardia-20> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.23770> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.175893> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2014.1383> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/claude-opus-5-5.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/active-inference-morphogenesis-falsifiable> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "A falsifiable form of active-inference morphogenesis" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.23770> dct:title "Normalized shape and location of perturbed craniofacial structures in the\n                    <i>Xenopus</i>\n                    tadpole reveal an innate ability to achieve correct morphology" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Vandenberg, Adams and Levin 2012, Normalized shape and location of perturbed craniofacial structures in the Xenopus tadpole" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.175893> dct:title "Adaptive correction of craniofacial defects in pre-metamorphic <i>Xenopus laevis</i> tadpoles involves thyroid hormone-independent tissue remodeling" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Pinet et al. 2019, Adaptive correction of craniofacial defects in pre-metamorphic Xenopus laevis tadpoles" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2014.1383> dct:title "Knowing one's place: a free-energy approach to pattern regulation" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Friston et al. 2015" .
}

